SICK::Bundle (402 lines): certificate, chain and key as PEM plus the facts openssl reads from the certificate.

Done when:
- Moo class: cert, chain, key as ro attributes; the facts behind _info (names, validity, fingerprint, subject, issuer) become a lazy attribute instead of a hand-filled hash slot;
- from_files reads through Path::Tiny;
- is_issued_by is unchanged in what it answers: the anchor is the root alone, the chain may run through intermediates the device did not send (skill sick-core, "Root and intermediates");
- t/12-bundle.t and everything that builds a bundle stays green; the Cisco suite too (it receives bundles in deploy).

SICK::Bundle is used by the SICK-Target-* distributions: constructor arguments and method names stay, additions only.

Bundle is Moo: cert Str, chain Maybe[Str], key with a coderef isa (Type::Tiny's explanation would repeat the key); BUILDARGS keeps the messages; facts lazy (_info, _sans, _common_name); from_files on Path::Tiny; is_issued_by untouched. prove -lr t and Cisco suite green; no dependency change; e2e not run.

